    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I solved my problem but the solution is bad because it doesn&#39;t generalize well.  <div><br></div><div>Given toy df:</div><div><br></div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">rainfall </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">frame</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">dates </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">as</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Date</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;2014-03-01&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)+</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">6</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#008\">as</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Date</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;2015-03-01&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)+</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">6</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rain </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> runif</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">14</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">4</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span></div></code></div><div><br><br></div><div>Suppose we want to compare the cumulative rainfall for the first week of March in each year.</div><div><br></div><div>This is close:</div><div><br></div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lubridate</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># for day() and year() fns</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">ggplot2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>ggplot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">rainfall</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> geom_step</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">aes</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> day</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">dates</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> cumsum</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">rain</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> color </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">as</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">factor</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">year</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">dates</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span></div></code></div><div><br><br></div><div>But that isn&#39;t quite it: we&#39;d like to have both months start at the same point for easy visual comparison.</div><div><br></div><div>Here&#39;s an ugly solution:</div><div><br></div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">tidyr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># for spread()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">dplyr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>df </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rainfall </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mutate</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">day </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> day</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">dates</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> year </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> year</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">dates</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">select</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">day</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> year</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rain</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> spread</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">year</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rain</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br>names</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">df</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;day&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;yr_2014&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;yr_2015&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># an ugly step, necessary b/c spread() turned years into var names in the new df</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>ggplot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">df</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> geom_step</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">aes</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> day</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> cumsum</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">yr_2014</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> color </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;blue&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> geom_step</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">aes</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> day</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> cumsum</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">yr_2015</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> color </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;red&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>This works, but i&#39;d like to avoid the un-tidying/ renaming/ etc of my data.</div><div><br></div><div>Is there a better way?</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
